# Arguments passed to the tierd daemon (word-split by systemd).
#
# The node joins through the seeds compiled into the binary, so no seed argument
# is required; membership is then learned via gossip.
#
# Default (join via the built-in seeds):
TIER_ARGS=run 7777
#
# An explicit seed can be added and is dialed in addition (IPv4/IPv6 literal,
# port as a separate token):
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 203.0.113.10 7777
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 2001:db8::10 7777
#
# The daemon binds the IPv6 wildcard (dual-stack), so it listens on both IPv6
# and IPv4 at the given port.
#
# Node configuration (roles, network, seeds, version policy) lives in
# /etc/tier/tierd.toml - see that file for the full, documented options. The
# environment variables below OVERRIDE the matching key in that file, for ad-hoc
# or orchestration use. Set them here only to override; otherwise edit the TOML.
#   TIER_CONFIG=/etc/tier/tierd.toml   # path to the config file (default shown)
#   TIER_ROLES=transmitter             # overrides config `roles`
#   TIER_NETWORK=testnet               # overrides config `network`
#   TIER_SEEDS=[fd00::2]:7777 10.0.0.2:7777   # overrides config `seeds`
#   TIER_VERSION_RANGE=1.4.0,1.5.0     # overrides config `version_range`
